  @.2304 text "Two HTTP URIs that are equivalent after normalization (using any method) can be assumed to identify the same resource, and any HTTP component MAY perform normalization. As a result, distinct resources SHOULD NOT be identified by HTTP URIs that are equivalent after normalization (using any method defined in "
  @.2309 link "Section 6.2" url="/rfc/rfc3986#section-6.2"
  @.2311 text " of ["
  @.2312 link "URI" url=$u1
  @.2314 text "])."
  @.2316 link "4.2.4. " url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-4.2.4"
  @.2318 link "Deprecation of userinfo in http(s) URIs" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-deprecation-of-userinfo-in-"
  @.2320 text "The URI generic syntax for authority also includes a userinfo subcomponent (["
  @.2322 link "URI" url=$u1
  @.2324 text "], "
  @.2325 link "Section 3.2.1" url="/rfc/rfc3986#section-3.2.1"
  @.2327 text ") for including user authentication information in the URI. In that subcomponent, the use of the format "user:password" is deprecated."
  @.2328 text "Some implementations make use of the userinfo component for internal configuration of authentication information, such as within command invocation options, configuration files, or bookmark lists, even though such usage might expose a user identifier or password.A sender MUST NOT"
  @.2331 text " generate the userinfo subcomponent (and its "@" delimiter) when an "http" or "https" URI reference is generated within a message as a target URI or field value."
  @.2332 text "Before making use of an "http" or "https" URI reference received from an untrusted source, a recipient "
  @.2333 text "SHOULD parse for userinfo and treat its presence as an error; it is likely being used to obscure the authority for the sake of phishing attacks."
  @.2335 link "4.2.5. " url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-4.2.5"
  @.2337 link "http(s) References with Fragment Identifiers" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-https-references-with-fragm"
  @.2339 text "Fragment identifiers allow for indirect identification of a secondary resource, independent of the URI scheme, as defined in "
