  @.6918 link "Byte Ranges" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-byte-ranges"
  @.6920 text "The "bytes" range unit is used to express subranges of a representation data's octet sequence. Each byte range is expressed as an integer range at some offset, relative to either the beginning ("
  @.6921 link "int-range" url=$u3
  @.6923 text ") or end ("
  @.6924 link "suffix-range" url=$u4
  @.6926 text ") of the representation data. Byte ranges do not use the "
  @.6927 link "other-range" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#rule.other-range"
  @.6929 text " specifier.The "
  @.6931 link "first-pos" url=$u3
  @.6933 text " value in a bytes "
  @.6934 link "int-range" url=$u3
  @.6936 text " gives the offset of the first byte in a range. The "
  @.6937 link "last-pos" url=$u3
  @.6939 text " value gives the offset of the last byte in the range; that is, the byte positions specified are inclusive. Byte offsets start at zero.If the representation data has a content coding applied, each byte range is calculated with respect to the encoded sequence of bytes, not the sequence of underlying bytes that would be obtained after decoding.Examples of bytes range specifiers:The first 500 bytes (byte offsets 0-499, inclusive):"
  @.6943 text "     bytes=0-499
"
  @.6944 text "The second 500 bytes (byte offsets 500-999, inclusive):"
  @.6945 text "     bytes=500-999
"
  @.6946 text "A client can limit the number of bytes requested without knowing the size of the "
  @.6947 link "selected representation" url=$u5
  @.6949 text ". If the "
  @.6950 link "last-pos" url=$u3
  @.6952 text " value is absent, or if the value is greater than or equal to the current length of the representation data, the byte range is interpreted as the remainder of the representation (i.e., the server replaces the value of "
  @.6953 link "last-pos" url=$u3
  @.6955 text " with a value that is one less than the current length of the selected representation).A client can refer to the last N bytes (N > 0) of the selected representation using a "
  @.6957 link "suffix-range" url=$u4
  @.6959 text ". If the selected representation is shorter than the specified "
  @.6960 link "suffix-length" url=$u4
  @.6962 text ", the entire representation is used.Additional examples, assuming a representation of length 10000:The final 500 bytes (byte offsets 9500-9999, inclusive):"
  @.6965 text "     bytes=-500
"
  @.6966 text "Or:"
  @.6967 text "     bytes=9500-
"
  @.6968 text "The first and last bytes only (bytes 0 and 9999):"
  @.6969 text "     bytes=0-0,-1
"
  @.6970 text "The first, middle, and last 1000 bytes:"
  @.6971 text "     bytes= 0-999, 4500-5499, -1000
"
  @.6972 text "Other valid (but not canonical) specifications of the second 500 bytes (byte offsets 500-999, inclusive):"
  @.6973 text "     bytes=500-600,601-999
     bytes=500-700,601-999
"
  @.6974 text "For a "
  @.6975 link "GET" url=$u6
  @.6977 text " request, a valid bytes "
  @.6978 link "range-spec" url=$u1
  @.6980 text " is "
  @.6981 link "satisfiable" url=$u7
  @.6983 text " if it is either:an "
  @.6985 link "int-range" url=$u3
  @.6987 text " with a "
  @.6988 link "first-pos" url=$u3
  @.6990 text " that is less than the current length of the selected representation ora "
  @.6992 link "suffix-range" url=$u4
  @.6994 text " with a non-zero "
  @.6995 link "suffix-length" url=$u4
  @.6997 text ".When a selected representation has zero length, the only "
  @.6999 link "satisfiable" url=$u7
  @.7001 text " form of "
  @.7002 link "range-spec" url=$u1
  @.7004 text " in a "
  @.7005 link "GET" url=$u6
  @.7007 text " request is a "
  @.7008 link "suffix-range" url=$u4
  @.7010 tex
