  @.2349 link "Section 4.3" url="/rfc/rfc3986#section-4.3"
  @.2351 text " of ["
  @.2352 link "URI" url=$u1
  @.2354 text "]"
  @.2355 text "), thus does not appear in the ABNF definitions for the "http" and "https" URI schemes above."
  @.2356 link "4.3. " url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-4.3"
  @.2358 link "Authoritative Access" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-authoritative-access"
  @.2360 text "Authoritative access refers to dereferencing a given identifier, for the sake of access to the identified resource, in a way that the client believes is authoritative (controlled by the resource owner). The process for determining whether access is granted is defined by the URI scheme and often uses data within the URI components, such as the authority component when the generic syntax is used. However, authoritative access is not limited to the identified mechanism."
  @.2361 link "Section 4.3.1" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#origin"
  @.2363 text " defines the concept of an origin as an aid to such uses, and the subsequent subsections explain how to establish that a peer has the authority to represent an origin.See "
