  @.4849 link "Content-Location" url=$u5
  @.4851 text " header field that has the same value as the POST's target URI ("
  @.4852 link "Section 8.7" url=$u5
  @.4854 text "). A cached POST response can be reused to satisfy a later GET or HEAD request. In contrast, a POST request cannot be satisfied by a cached POST response because POST is potentially unsafe; see "
  @.
