  @.7150 text "to indicate that it supports byte range requests for that target resource, thereby encouraging its use by the client for future partial requests on the same request path. Range units are defined in "
  @.7151 link "Section 14.1" url=$u1
  @.7153 text ".A client MAY generate range requests regardless of having received an Accept-Ranges field. The information only provides advice for the sake of improving performance and reducing unnecessary network transfers.Conversely, a client MUST NOT assume that receiving an Accept-Ranges field means that future range requests will return partial responses. The content might change, the server might only support range requests at certain times or under certain conditions, or a different intermediary might process the next request.A server that does not support any kind of range request for the target resource MAY send"
  @.7163 text "Accept-Ranges: none
"
  @.7164 text "to advise the client not to attempt a range request on the same request path. The range unit "none" is reserved for this purpose."
  @.7165 text "The Accept-Ranges field MAY be sent in a trailer section, but is preferred to be sent as a header field because the information is particularly useful for restarting large information transfers that have failed in mid-content (before the trailer section is received)."
  @.7168 link "14.4. " url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-14.4"
  @.7170 link "Content-Range" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-content-range"
  @.7172 text "The "Content-Range" header field is sent in a single part "
  @.7173 link "206 (Partial Content)" url=$u2
  @.7175 text " response to indicate the partial range of the "
  @.7176 link "selected representation" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#selected.representation"
  @.7178 text " enclosed as the message content, sent in each part of a multipart 206 response to indicate the range enclosed within each body part ("
  @.7179 link "Section 14.6" url=$u3
  @.7181 text "), and sent in "
  @.7182 link "416 (Range Not Satisfiable)" url=$u4
  @.7184 text " responses to provide information about the selected representation."
  @.7185 text "  Content-Range       = range-unit SP
                        ( range-resp / unsatisfied-range )

  range-resp          = incl-range "/" ( complete-length / "*" )
  incl-range          = first-pos "-" last-pos
  unsatisfied-range   = "*/" complete-length

  complete-length     = 1*DIGIT
"
  @.7186 text "If a "
  @.7187 link "206 (Partial Content)" url=$u2
  @.7189 text " response contains a "
  @.7190 link "Content-Range" url=$u5
