  @.7761 text "A response might transfer only a subrange of a representation if the connection closed prematurely or if the request used one or more Range specifications. After several such transfers, a client might have received several ranges of the same representation. These ranges can only be safely combined if they all have in common the same strong validator ("
  @.7762 link "Section 8.8.1" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#weak.and.strong.validators"
  @.7764 text ").A client that has received multiple partial responses to GET requests on a target resource MAY combine those responses into a larger continuous range if they share the same strong validator.If the most recent response is an incomplete "
  @.7769 link "200 (OK)" url=$u1
  @.7771 text " response, then the header fields of that response are used for any combined response and replace those of the matching stored responses.If the most recent response is a "
  @.7773 link "206 (Partial Content)" url=$u2
  @.7775 text " response and at least one of the matching stored responses is a "
  @.7776 link "200 (OK)" url=$u1
  @.7778 text ", then the combined response header fields consist of the most recent 200 response's header fields. If all of the matching stored responses are 206 responses, then the stored response with the most recent header fields is used as the source of header fields for the combined response, except that the client MUST use other header fields provided in the new response, aside from "
  @.7781 link "Content-Range" url=$u3
  @.7783 text ", to replace all instances of the corresponding header fields in the stored response.The combined response content consists of the union of partial content ranges within the new response and all of the matching stored responses. If the union consists of the entire range of the representation, then the client MUST process the combined response as if it were a complete "
  @.7787 link "200 (OK)" url=$u1
  @.7789 text " response, including a "
  @.7790 link "Content-Length" url=$u4
  @.7792 text " header field that reflects the complete length. Otherwise, the client MUST process the set of continuous ranges as one of the following: an incomplete "
  @.7795 link "200 (OK)" url=$u1
  @.7797 text " response if the combined response is a prefix of the representation, a single "
  @.7798 link "206 (Partial Content)" url=$u2
  @.7800 text " response containing "multipart/byteranges" content, or multiple "
  @.7801 link "206 (Partial Content)" url=$u2
  @.7803 text " responses, each with one continuous range that is indicated by a "
